:: Bailey Halloween Guest Avery
<<npc Avery>><<person1>>

You scan the room for any faces you recognize. A hand comes to rest on your shoulder, you turn and see Avery. <<His>> clothes are elegant, but <<hes>> not wearing a costume. It makes <<him>> stand out.
<br><br>

"<<pcpetname "Avery">>," <<he>> says to you, beaming. "I didn't think anyone worthwhile would be here. I'm glad I was wrong."
<br><br>

<<He>> looks across the room at Bailey before <<he>> redirects <<his>> attention to you.
<br><br>

"I heard you would be here, but I didn't think your <<if $avery_mansion>>old <</if>>caretaker would actually bring you." <<He>> seems to smile at the thought. "How are you?"
<br><br>

<<link [[Schmooze|Bailey Halloween Guest Avery Schmooze]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay quiet|Bailey Halloween Guest Avery Quiet]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Bailey Halloween Guest Avery Schmooze
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<person1>>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"I-I'm doing well. Much better now that you're here," you say. "I was worried I wasn't going to know anyone."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"I'm very well, Avery. It is a relief to see a familiar face," you say. "May I join you for a while?"
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You move closer to Avery. "I'm all right. I didn't know anyone else here."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"I'm good," you say. "Now I have someone worth talking to."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"I'm good. I'm happy to see you," you say. "I didn't think I'd see anyone I know."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You glance at the other guests before facing Avery. "I'm better now. Nobody else here has been worth the effort."
<<else>>
	"Good. I'm glad to see you," you say. "I didn't see anyone else I recognized."
<</if>>
<br><br>

Avery's smile widens. "I was only planning to make a quick appearance here, but you're going to make me change my mind."
<br><br>

The two of you spend some time talking about <<print either("you growing up at the Bailey Orphanage", "how Avery's work has been going", "Bailey's particularities with food")>>.<<baileyHalloweenMood 1>>
<br><br>

"I have some old friends I need to catch up with." Avery says after awhile. "Maybe I'll see you before I head out."
<br><br>

<<He>> gives your shoulder a squeeze before <<he>> goes.
<br><br>

<<link [[Back to the gala|Bailey Halloween Gala Menu]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Bailey Halloween Guest Avery Quiet
<<effects>>
<<person1>>

You say nothing to Avery.<<npcincr Avery love -1>><<llove "Avery">>
<br><br>

Avery hovers near you in silence for awhile, scanning through the crowds.
<br><br>

"I have some old friends I need to catch up with." Avery says after awhile. "Maybe I'll see you before I head out."
<br><br>

<<link [[Back to the gala|Bailey Halloween Gala Menu]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


:: Bailey Halloween Guest Quinn

You scan the room for any faces you recognize. A booming voice carries past your shoulder, "There <<pshe>> <<pverb 'is' 'are'>>, the orphan of the hour!"
<br><br>
<<if C.npc.Quinn.init is 1>>
	<<npc Quinn>><<person1>>
	You turn around and see Mayor Quinn, smiling at you. <<He>> makes <<his>> way right up to you and places a hand on your shoulder.
<<else>>
	<<npc Quinn>><<person1>>
	A middle-aged <<personsimple>> is smiling right at you. <<He>> makes <<his>> way to you and grasps your hand, shaking it. "It's wonderful to meet you. I'm Quinn." <<takeHandholdingVirginity "Quinn" null null true>>
<</if>>
<<He>> gestures broadly towards the venue. "Look at how many people have come to wish the orphanage well. I've never seen Bailey pull numbers like this on <<nnpc_his "Bailey">> own. You must be <<nnpc_his "Bailey">> lucky charm."
<br><br>

<<link [[Schmooze|Bailey Halloween Guest Quinn Schmooze]]>><</link>>
<br>
<<link [[Stay quiet|Bailey Halloween Guest Quinn Quiet]]>><</link>>
<br>


:: Bailey Halloween Guest Quinn Schmooze
<<effects>><<speechresolve>>
<<person1>>

<<if (_speechAttitudeResolved is "meek" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "shy")>>
	"It's good to see you, Mayor Quinn," you say. "Y-You didn't have to come out just for us."
	<<elseif (_speechAttitudeResolved is "polite" or _speechAttitudeResolved is "flamboyant")>>
	"Mayor Quinn, thank you for attending," you say. "Your presence means a great deal to the orphanage."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "docile">>
	You wait until Quinn finishes speaking with another guest. "Thank you for coming, Mayor."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "confident">>
	"Mayor Quinn, I'm glad you made it," you say. "I hope the evening earns your support."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "bratty">>
	"It's good to see you, Mayor Quinn," you say. "Bet you have to show up to lots of events you don't want to bother with."
<<elseif _speechAttitudeResolved is "cruel">>
	You step into Quinn's path. "Mayor, I hope you're here to give more than a speech. The orphanage needs money."
<<else>>
	"It's good to see you, Mayor Quinn," you say. "I didn't think you'd come just for this."
<</if>>
<br><br>

"Nonsense, I wouldn't miss it for the world," <<he>> replies. "Bailey is one of the most hardworking and well-established philanthropists in this town. The least I can do is show up when invited."
<br><br>

The two of you talk about <<print either("growing up at the Bailey orphanage", "how Bailey must have worked hard to set up this event", "the weather and other pleasantries")>>.<<baileyHalloweenMood 1>>
<br><br>

Quinn checks <<his>> watch. "It was lovely chatting with you. Have a good night."
<br><br>

<<link [[Back to the gala|Bailey Halloween Gala Menu]]>><<endevent>><</link>>
<br>


